 "summary": "The order-one Hadamard factorization, partial-fraction corollaries, inverse-square summability bridge and divisor-product examples have no Mathlib or TauCeti counterpart, and they build on the existing divisor-factorization, divisorProductOne, Landau, zero-summability and polynomial-Liouville APIs; the zero-free case in GrowthOrder/Exponential.lean (OrderLE.eq_affine_of_cexp) does not cover them. The small calculus helpers (affine form of is_const_of_deriv_eq_zero, logDeriv of g * exp \u2218 L) are absent from Mathlib and are proved from Mathlib's lemmas; the promoted notMem_divisor_support_of_ne_zero replaces the old private helper at every call site.",
